n\tProcess ID:\t\t0x2b8\r\r\n\tProcess Name:\t\tC:\\Windows\\System32\\lsass.exe\r\nevt-01778|DC01.corp.example|WS-06$||The handle to an object was closed.\r\r\n\r\r\nSubject :\r\r\n\tSecurity ID:\t\tS-1-5-21-4228717743-1032521047-1810997296-1113\r\r\n\tAccount Name:\t\tWS-06$\r\r\n\tAccount Domain:\t\tCORP\r\r\n\tLogon ID:\t\t0x697C9CB\r\r\n\r\r\nObject:\r\r\n\tObject Server:\t\tSecurity Account Manager\r\r\n\tHandle ID:\t\t0x219e3751060\r\r\n\r\r\nProcess Information:\r\r\n\tProcess ID:\t\t0x2b8\r\r\n\tProcess Name:\t\tC:\\Windows\\System32\\lsass.exe\r\nevt-01782|DC01.corp.example|-|WS-06$|An account was successfully logged on.\r\r\n\r\r\nSubject:\r\r\n\tSecurity ID:\t\tS-1-0-0\r\r\n\tAccount Name:\t\t-\r\r\n\tAccount Domain:\t\t-\r\r\n\tLogon ID:\t\t0x0\r\r\n\r\r\nLogon Information:\r\r\n\tLogon Type:\t\t3\r\r\n\tRestricted Admin Mode:\t-\r\r\n\tVirtual Account:\t\tNo\r\r\n\tElevated Token:\t\tYes\r\r\n\r\r\nImpersonation Level:\t\tImpersonation\r\r\n\r\r\nNew Logon:\r\r\n\tSecurity ID:\t\tS-1-5-21-4228717743-1032521047-1810997296-1113\r\r\n\tAccount Name:\t\tWS-06$\r\r\n\tAccount Domain:\t\tCORP.LOCAL\r\r\n\tLogon ID:\t\t0x697CA68\r\r\n\tLinked Logon ID:\t\t0x0\r\r\n\tNetwork Account Name:\t-\r\r\n\tNetwork Account Domain:\t-\r\r\n\tLogon GUID:\t\t{4020946f-1fe5-e4d3-ff9f-97f02c0b553d}\r\r\n\r\r\nProcess Information:\r\r\n\tProcess ID:\t\t0x0\r\r\n\tProcess Name:\t\t-\r\r\n\r\r\nNetwork Information:\r\r\n\tWorkstation Name:\t-\r\r\n\tSource Network Address:\t172.18.39.6\r\r\n\tSource Port:\t\t51297\r\r\n\r\r\nDetailed Authentication Information:\r\r\n\tLogon Process:\t\tKerberos\r\r\n\tAuthentication Package:\tKerberos\r\r\n\tTransited Services:\t-\r\r\n\tPackage Name (NTLM only):\t-\r\r\n\tKey Length:\t\t0\r\r\n\r\r\nThis event is generated when a logon session is created. It is generated on the computer that was accessed.\r\r\n\r\r\nThe subject fields indicate the account on the local system which requested the logon. This is most commonly a service such as the Server service, or a local process such as Winlogon.exe or Services.exe.\r\r\n\r\r\nThe logon type field indicates the kind of logon that occurred. The most common types are 2 (interactive) and 3 (network).\r\r\n\r\r\nThe New Logon fields indicate the account for whom the new logon was created, i.e. the account that was logged on.\r\r\n\r\r\nThe network fields indicate where a remote logon request originated. Workstation name is not always available and may be left blank in some cases.\r\r\n\r\r\nThe impersonation level field indicates the extent to which a process in the logon session can impersonate.\r\r\n\r\r\nThe authentication information fields provide detailed information about this specific logon request.\r\r\n\t- Logon GUID is a unique identifier that can be used to correlate this event with a KDC event.\r\r\n\t- Transited services indicate which intermediate ser\r\nevt-01783|DC01.corp.example|-|WS-06$|Group membership information.\r\r\n\r\r\nSubject:\r\r\n\tSecurity ID:\t\tS-1-0-0\r\r\n\tAccount Name:\t\t-\r\r\n\tAccount Domain:\t\t-\r\r\n\tLogon ID:\t\t0x0\r\r\n\r\r\nLogon Type:\t\t\t3\r\r\n\r\r\nNew Logon:\r\r\n\tSecurity ID:\t\tS-1-5-21-4228717743-1032521047-1810997296-1113\r\r\n\tAccount Name:\t\tWS-06$\r\r\n\tAccount Domain:\t\tCORP.LOCAL\r\r\n\tLogon ID:\t\t0x697CA68\r\r\n\r\r\nEvent in sequence:\t\t1 of 1\r\r\n\r\r\nGroup Membership:\t\t\t\r\r\n\t\t%{S-1-5-21-4228717743-1032521047-1810997296-515}\r\r\n\t\t%{S-1-1-0}\r\r\n\t\t%{S-1-5-32-554}\r\r\n\t\t%{S-1-5-32-545}\r\r\n\t\t%{S-1-5-32-555}\r\r\n\t\t%{S-1-5-2}\r\r\n\t\t%{S-1-5-11}\r\r\n\t\t%{S-1-5-15}\r\r\n\t\t%{S-1-18-1}\r\r\n\t\t%{S-1-16-8448}\r\r\n\r\r\nThe subject fields indicate the account on the local system which requested the logon. This is most commonly a service such as the Server service, or a local process such as Winlogon.exe or Services.exe.\r\r\n\r\r\nThe logon type field indicates the kind of logon that occurred. The most common types are 2 (interactive) and 3 (network).\r\r\n\r\r\nThe New Logon fields indicate the account for whom the new logon was created, i.e. the account that was logged on.\r\r\n\r\r\nThis event is generated when the Audit Group Membership subcategory is configured.  The Logon ID field can be used to correlate this event with the corresponding user logon event as well as to any other security audit events generated during this logon session.\r\nevt-01784|DC01.corp.example||WS-06$|An account was logged off.\r\r\n\r\r\nSubject:\r\r\n\tSecurity ID:\t\t"]
[115.789552, "o", "S-1-5-21-4228717743-1032521047-1810997296-1113\r\r\n\tAccount Name:\t\tWS-06$\r\r\n\tAccount Domain:\t\tCORP\r\r\n\tLogon ID:\t\t0x697CA68\r\r\n\r\r\nLogon Type:\t\t\t3\r\r\n\r\r\nThis event is generated when a logon session is destroyed. It may be positively correlated with a logon event using the Logon ID value. Logon IDs are only unique between reboots on the same computer.\r\nevt-01786|DC01.corp.example|-|WS-06$|An account was successfully logged on.\r\r\n\r\r\nSubject:\r\r\n\tSecurity ID:\t\tS-1-0-0\r\r\n\tAccount Name:\t\t-\r\r\n\tAccount Domain:\t\t-\r\r\n\tLogon ID:\t\t0x0\r\r\n\r\r\nLogon Information:\r\r\n\tLogon Type:\t\t3\r\r\n\tRestricted Admin Mode:\t-\r\r\n\tVirtual Account:\t\tNo\r\r\n\tElevated Token:\t\tYes\r\r\n\r\r\nImpersonation Level:\t\tImpersonation\r\r\n\r\r\nNew Logon:\r\r\n\tSecurity ID:\t\tS-1-5-21-4228717743-1032521047-1810997296-1113\r\r\n\tAccount Name:\t\tWS-06$\r\r\n\tAccount Domain:\t\tCORP.LOCAL\r\r\n\tLogon ID:\t\t0x697CA81\r\r\n\tLinked Logon ID:\t\t0x0\r\r\n\tNetwork Account Name:\t-\r\r\n\tNetwork Account Domain:\t-\r\r\n\tLogon GUID:\t\t{4020946f-1fe5-e4d3-ff9f-97f02c0b553d}\r\r\n\r\r\nProcess Information:\r\r\n\tProcess ID:\t\t0x0\r\r\n\tProcess Name:\t\t-\r\r\n\r\r\nNetwork Information:\r\r\n\tWorkstation Name:\t-\r\r\n\tSource Network Address:\t172.18.39.6\r\r\n\tSource Port:\t\t51298\r\r\n\r\r\nDetailed Authentication Information:\r\r\n\tLogon Process:\t\tKerberos\r\r\n\tAuthentication Package:\tKerberos\r\r\n\tTransited Services:\t-\r\r\n\tPackage Name (NTLM only):\t-\r\r\n\tKey Length:\t\t0\r\r\n\r\r\nThis event is generated when a logon session is created. It is generated on the computer that was accessed.\r\r\n\r\r\nThe subject fields indicate the account on the local system which requested the logon. This is most commonly a service such as the Server service, or a local process such as Winlogon.exe or Services.exe.\r\r\n"]
[115.790167, "o", "\r\r\nThe logon type field indicates the kind of logon that occurred. The most common types are 2 (interactive) and 3 (network).\r\r\n\r\r\nThe New Logon fields indicate the account for whom the new logon was created, i.e. the account that was logged on.\r\r\n\r\r\nThe network fields indicate where a remote logon request originated. Workstation name is not always available and may be left blank in some cases.\r\r\n\r\r\nThe impersonation level field indicates the extent to which a process in the logon session can impersonate.\r\r\n\r\r\nThe authentication information fields provide detailed information about this specific logon request.\r\r\n\t- Logon GUID is a unique identifier that can be used to correlate this event with a KDC event.\r\r\n\t- Transited services indicate which intermediate ser\r\nevt-01787|DC01.corp.example|-|WS-06$|Group membership information.\r\r\n\r\r\nSubject:\r\r\n\tSecurity ID:\t\tS-1-0-0\r\r\n\tAccount Name:\t\t-\r\r\n\tAccount Domain:\t\t-\r\r\n\tLogon ID:\t\t0x0\r\r\n\r\r\nLogon Type:\t\t\t3\r\r\n\r\r\nNew Logon:\r\r\n\tSecurity ID:\t\tS-1-5-21-4228717743-1032521047-1810997296-1113\r\r\n\tAccount Name:\t\tWS-06$\r\r\n\tAccount Domain:\t\tCORP.LOCAL\r\r\n\tLogon ID:\t\t0x697CA81\r\r\n\r\r\nEvent in sequence:\t\t1 of 1\r\r\n\r\r\nGroup Membership:\t\t\t\r\r\n\t\t%{S-1-5-21-4228717743-1032521047-1810997296-515}\r\r\n\t\t%{S-1-1-0}\r\r\n\t\t%{S-1-5-32-554}\r\r\n\t\t%{S-1-5-32-545}\r\r\n\t\t%{S-1-5-32-555}\r\r\n\t\t%{S-1-5-2}\r\r\n\t\t%{S-1-5-11}\r\r\n\t\t%{S-1-5-15}\r\r\n\t\t%{S-1-18-1}\r\r\n\t\t%{S-1-16-8448}\r\r\n\r\r\nThe subject fields indicate the account on the local system which requested the logon. This is most commonly a service such as the Server service, or a local process such as Winlogon.exe or Services.exe.\r\r\n\r\r\nThe logon type field indicates the kind of logon that occurred. The most common types are 2 (interactive) and 3 (network).\r\r\n\r\r\nThe New Logon fields indicate the account for whom the new logon was created, i.e. the account that was logged on.\r\r\n\r\r\nThis event is generated when the Audit Group Membership subcategory is configured.  The Logon ID field can be used to correlate this event with the corresponding user logon event as well as to any other security audit events generated during this logon session.\r\nevt-01816|DC01.corp.example|||Audit only mode is currently enabled for remote calls to the SAM database.\r\r\nThe following client would have been normally denied access:\r\r\nClient SID: S-1-5-21-4228717743-1032521047-1810997296-1113 from network address: 172.18.39.6. \r\r\nFor more information please see http://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?LinkId=787651.\r\nevt-01818|DC01.corp.example|||Audit only mode is currently enabled for remote calls to the SAM database.\r\r\nThe following client would have been normally denied access:\r\r\nClient SID: S-1-5-21-4228717743-1032521047-1810997296-1113 from network address: 172.18.39.6. \r\r\nFor more information please see http://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?LinkId=787651.\r\nevt-01820|DC01.corp.example|||Audit only mode is currently enabled for remote calls to the SAM database.\r\r\nThe following client would have been normally denied access:\r\r\nClient SID: S-1-5-21-4228717743-1032521047-1810997296-1113 from network address: 172.18.39.6. \r\r\nFor more information please see http://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?LinkId=787651.\r\nevt-01822|DC01.corp.example|||Audit only mode is currently enabled for remote calls to the SAM database.\r\r\nThe following client would have been normally denied access:\r\r\nClient SID: S-1-5-21-4228717743-1032521047-1810997296-1113 from network address: 172.18.39.6. \r\r\nFor more information please see http://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?LinkId=787651.\r\nevt-01825|DC01.corp.example|||Audit only mode is currently enabled for remote calls to the SAM database.\r\r\nThe following client would have been normally denied access:\r\r\nClient SID: S-1-5-21-4228717743-1032521047-1810997296-1113 fr